  "note": "IR-1278. A temporal_clause node carries no declaration: structurally equal clauses share one node, so the declared name is carried per claim occurrence in the temporal_clause_names row (FR-322 \"Temporal clause names\"). Each case is an RFC 6902 patch on `base`. The token \"<clause>\" in a patch value stands for the NodeRef of the base package's one temporal_clause node (graph index 8) and \"<node 9>\" for the NodeRef of graph node 9, a node that is not a temporal clause. A package with a second occurrence also carries that occurrence's temporal_bindings row (the binding is per occurrence). `schema` is `valid` or `invalid`; `expected` is admitted or the refusal code, optional cause and RFC 6901 locus. The row checks run per row in array order (declaration, occurrence, repeated key, order) and coverage last.",
